course: dictionary
lesson: 11760
title: Baptists, a group of churches
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: «Baptists» is a plural noun. It names a group of people, and one member is a Baptist. In this lesson it is a word about churches and religion, so it has a capital letter.
explain: «The Baptists in our town meet on Sunday morning.» The clues are town, meet and Sunday. A group that meets on Sunday in a church is a religious group, so Baptists must mean members of a Christian church.
explain: Other words in a text can give you more clues. Hymns, Bible reading, sermon and prayer all belong to a church service. When you see these words near an unknown word, ask: what kind of place or group would do all of these things?
fact: «Baptists» are members of Christian churches.
fact: Baptist churches baptise only believers who are old enough to choose for themselves.
fact: Baptism is usually done by full immersion, which means going fully under water.
fact: Each Baptist church largely runs itself.
fact: Baptists are found in the USA, Wales, England, Australia, Canada and Africa, and «Martin Luther King Jr.» was a famous Baptist.
exercise: «The Baptists in our town meet on Sunday morning.» What are Baptists in this sentence? | Teachers who only work in the mornings | *Members of a Christian church | People who run the bus company | People who sell fish at the market
exercise: Baptist services include hymns, Bible reading, a sermon and prayer. Which of these is NOT part of a Baptist service? | *Football matches | Prayer | Bible reading | Hymns
exercise: «Southern Baptists are a big group in the USA.» Where are many Southern Baptists found? | Only in the town hall | In a small village with no churches | On a ship at sea | *In the USA
test: What does it mean that Baptists baptise only believers old enough to choose? | Everyone must be baptised at birth | Baptism is never done in their churches | Babies are always baptised first | *Only people old enough to choose are baptised
test: What does full immersion mean? | *Going fully under water | Singing in a choir | Reading a long sermon | Sprinkling a few drops on the head
exam: «Martin Luther King Jr. was a famous Baptist.» Which of these names was also a famous Baptist? | Charles Darwin | William Shakespeare | *Martin Luther King Jr. | Isaac Newton
